<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BPI Q1 profit up 4.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BPI Q1 profit up 4.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ending March 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	    4.7    vs    4.5</p>
<p>    Banking income	    25.9    vs   15.0</p>
<p>    Financial margin	  18.4    vs    8.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax cashflow	   8.7    vs    8.3</p>
<p>    Structural costs	  17.4    vs    7.2</p>
<p>Commission and other</p>
<p>    income			 6.2    vs    2.4</p>
<p>Note - Banco Portugues de Investimento is company name.  </p>
<p>    ROE (pct)		   22.5 (no comparison)</p>
<p>    Total Assets	   3,010.0  vs 2,889.0 (Dec 96)</p>
<p>    Client loans	   1,201.0  vs 1,192.0 (Dec 96)</p>
<p>    Deposits		 1,823    vs 1,790.0 (Dec 96)</p>
<p>Credits more than</p>
<p>    90 days overdue	 3.1 pct vs   3.2 pct</p>
<p>    Risk provisions     143.0 pct vs 107.0 pct</p>
<p>The Bank said that the first quarter results were not directly comparable with those of the same quarter 1996 because of the subsequent purchase of Banco de Fomento &amp; Exterior.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
